 ## Overview
-This method converts a triangulated surface mesh into a 3D distance field by computing the Euclidean distance from each voxel center to the closest point on the mesh surface, with sign assignment based on surface normals or topological containment [S1, unofficial][S3, unofficial][S4]. It enables rendering and isosurfacing of explicit CAD or scanned meshes using implicit surface techniques, such as interval-arithmetic bisection or marching cubes [S1, unofficial][S4]. Unlike [Slice-based SDF Voxelization](1736-slice-based-sdf-voxelization.md), which processes depth slices, this method operates directly on geometric primitives (triangles) [S1, unofficial].
+This method converts a triangulated surface mesh into a 3D distance field by computing the Euclidean distance from each voxel center to the closest point on the mesh surface, with sign assignment based on surface normals or topological containment [S1, unofficial][S3, unofficial][S4]. It enables rendering and isosurfacing of explicit CAD or scanned meshes using implicit surface techniques, such as interval-arithmetic bisection or marching cubes [S1, unofficial][S4]. Unlike [Slice-based SDF Voxelization](1736-slice-based-sdf-voxelization.md), which processes depth slices, this method operates directly on geometric primitives (triangles) [S1, unofficial]. Builds on [Signed Distance Field (SDF) Generation from Scanned Surfaces](854-signed-distance-field-sdf-generation-from-scanned-surfaces.md).
 
